export const SETUP_PROMPT: string = "Set up my LofiStack 90 Day Build Challenge component gallery from scratch.\n\nStack: Next.js (latest, App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 + ESLint, npm. Extra deps: lucide-react, clsx, tailwind-merge, shiki.\n\nCreate:\n1. lib/utils.ts: cn() helper (clsx + tailwind-merge).\n2. lib/registry.ts: typed array of every component { slug, name, type, week, description, addedAt } plus getComponent(slug). Type is one of: button, form, card, modal, navbar, table, loader, section, chart, input.\n3. app/page.tsx: gallery homepage. Site title \"<My Name> Component Gallery\", one-line intro, filter chips by type, responsive grid of cards linking to /components/<slug> with name, type badge and week number. Shows \"x / 30 components\" progress.\n4. components/gallery/ComponentPage.tsx: the shared layout every component page uses. Props: title, type, description, children (live preview), code (usage snippet string), props?: { name, type, default?, description }[]. Layout: back link to gallery, title + type badge, Preview / Code tabs, preview stage with a subtle dotted background, viewport toggle (375 / 768 / full) and a light/dark toggle for the preview only, then a props table and the usage code block.\n5. components/gallery/CodeBlock.tsx: syntax-highlighted code using shiki in a server component, with a client copy button that shows a \"Copied\" state.\n6. Routing: every component gets its own static folder app/components/<slug>/page.tsx (no catch-all route), so each has a direct link like /components/glass-button. Add generateMetadata/title per page.\n7. Root layout: header with site name, link to the public GitHub repo and a theme toggle (system default, class-based dark mode via @custom-variant dark in globals.css, no flash on load); footer \"Built for the LofiStack 90 Day Build Challenge\".\n8. A 404 page and a sitemap.ts that lists every component route.\n9. README.md with a table of components (#, Name, Type, Week, Live link) and how to run locally.\n10. Deploy-ready for Vercel. Add a README section for GitHub Pages (output: 'export', basePath, images.unoptimized) in case I switch.\n\nQuality bar: responsive at 375 / 768 / 1280px, visible focus states, WCAG AA contrast in both themes, zero lint errors, `npm run build` passes.\n\nFinally, give me the exact terminal commands to: create the project, init git, push to a new public GitHub repo, and deploy on Vercel.";

